      "author": "Vyacheslav Argenberg",
      "credit": "Own work",
      "attribution": "",
      "description": "This sculpture represents a highly symbolic and profound form of Shiva known as Ekapada-Trimurti or Trinity. The central figure is Shiva in Hanuman style, in his unmanifested form. Emerging from the sides of the central Shiva figure are the deities Vishnu and Brahma. It represents Shiva as the ultimate cosmic pillar (Axis Mundi), the central axis of the universe and the ultimate manifestation of the Absolute from which creation, preservation, and destruction originate, and into which they ultimately dissolve. The statue is heavily adorned with red powder (sindoor or kumkum) commonly used in Hindu ritual worship. Meenakshi Temple. Madurai, Tamil Nadu, India.",
