      "description": "Meenakshi Temple in Madurai, 6th to 14th century, a historic Hindu temple renowned for its vibrant Dravidian architecture. Meenakshi is a form of Parvati and her consort Shiva. In Shaivism, the temple is amongst the four most important of the pilgrimage sites and is as important as the city of Varanasi itself. The entrance into the Shaivite sanctum sanctorum of the temple is guarded by at least two Brahmin priests, sometimes four. Entry is generally forbidden to any foreigner, but if you’re lucky enough to show genuine appreciation of Hindu culture, you may be able to get through. Meenakshi Temple. Madurai, Tamil Nadu, India.",
